ogic signals between serial and parallel formats, or to move the position of the data bits within a digital word. Typically implemented using an array of flip-flops integrated into one device, shift registers are a common component of more highly integrated logic devices, though they remain available for applications such as I/O expansion where the function in a discrete form may prove useful.","ChildCategories":[]}]}]},"ManufacturerLeadWeeks":"20","ManufacturerPublicQuantity":0,"Series":{"Id":505,"Name":"TPIC"},"Classifications":{"ReachStatus":"REACH Unaffected","RohsStatus":"ROHS3 Compliant","MoistureSensitivityLevel":"1  (Unlimited)","ExportControlClassNumber":"EAR99","HtsusCode":"8542.39.0070"},"OtherNames":["296-1351-2","296-1351-1","296-1351-1-NDR","296-1351-6","2156-TPIC6B595DWR","296-1351-2-NDR","TEXTISTPIC6B595DWR"]},"AccountIdUsed":0,"CustomerIdUsed":0}